  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The AI Horizon & The Observable Control Plane. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 30: Adam Lear from UGtastic Archive (2013).",
  "Recorded during Adam Lear's tenure as Community Manager at Stack Exchange, exploring community governance models that outlast individual maintainers.",
  "How do large-scale technical communities self-govern without authoritarian collapse? What role do meta feedback loops play in setting norms for millions of programmers? What principles guided Adam Lear when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "Roll archive footage (YouTube ID: Hf_wKDbl2mQ). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "Autonomous multi-agent ecosystems require verifiable governance, clear moderation rules, and self-correcting mechanisms exactly like human communities. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
